WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.471
Toki: Vera, who actually picks the next word?

00:00:02.871 --> 00:00:06.949
Vera: Nobody, yet. The network gives every token a score: a logit.

00:00:07.349 --> 00:00:10.383
Vera: Then a separate, simple step chooses one: the sampler.

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:12.824
Toki: So the network scores, and the sampler picks.

00:00:14.424 --> 00:00:15.713
Toki: But a score isn't a chance.

00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:21.274
Vera: Softmax makes them probabilities that add up to one. “Practice” gets almost 32%.

00:00:21.674 --> 00:00:22.562
Toki: From a real model?

00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:25.527
Vera: Hand-set words and scores. Real maths.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:29.128
Toki: And the “creativity” setting in AI tools?

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:32.919
Vera: Temperature. The scores are divided by it before softmax.

00:00:33.319 --> 00:00:37.623
Vera: Turn it down: the favourite takes over. At zero, always the top token.

00:00:38.023 --> 00:00:38.560
Toki: Reliable!

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.922
Vera: Repeatable. Also dull, and prone to loops. Turn it up: the bars flatten.

00:00:44.322 --> 00:00:46.642
Toki: So even “banana” gets a chance? Chaos.

00:00:48.242 --> 00:00:49.451
Toki: How do you keep the nonsense out?

00:00:49.851 --> 00:00:53.469
Vera: Cut the long tail. Top-k keeps a fixed number, say three.

00:00:53.869 --> 00:00:56.752
Vera: Top-p keeps the smallest set adding up to 80%.

00:00:57.152 --> 00:00:57.941
Toki: What's the difference?

00:00:58.341 --> 00:01:03.208
Vera: Top-p adapts. Sure, like “Paris”: one word. Unsure: more.

00:01:04.808 --> 00:01:06.576
Toki: Say it picks “practice”. Then what?

00:01:06.976 --> 00:01:09.643
Vera: The pick joins the text, and the whole model runs again.

00:01:10.043 --> 00:01:11.630
Toki: The whole model? Every time?

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.899
Vera: Every token. That's autoregressive generation.

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:17.264
Toki: So that's why answers appear word by word!

00:01:18.864 --> 00:01:20.948
Toki: Vera, can I turn these dials myself?

00:01:21.348 --> 00:01:25.370
Vera: Drag them in the Sampling chapter, or play The Dial in the game: you're the sampler.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.601
Toki: Mission one: “make it boring”. Finally, something I'm good at.
